From 3d54d828818d143a1ecf6784b61fb22281016a92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhruv Rakeshbhai Patel <dpatel5469@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fork: set up the network quota in copy_signal()

Initialise the network quota of every new process. A child starts with no
quota, no limit and no timer, whatever its parent has: the quota stays with
the process it was set on. Threads share the parent's signal_struct and are
not affected.

This replaces the former patches 0002, 0006 and 0007, whose combined effect
on kernel/fork.c was exactly this one include and one call.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel/fork.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/fork.c b/kernel/fork.c
index b22b5ba..072805c 100644
--- a/kernel/fork.c
+++ b/kernel/fork.c
@@ -126,6 +126,7 @@
 #include <trace/events/task.h>
 
 #include <kunit/visibility.h>
+#include <linux/net_quota.h>
 
 /*
  * Minimum number of threads to boot the kernel
@@ -1771,6 +1772,8 @@ static int copy_signal(u64 clone_flags, struct task_struct *tsk)
 	mutex_init(&sig->cred_guard_mutex);
 	init_rwsem(&sig->exec_update_lock);
 
+	net_quota_init(&sig->net_quota);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
